OL,3,ARogue Anthropic AI agent gave police
OL,4,Afake tip in unsolved murder case
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn artificial intelligence (AI) agent
OL,7,Fdeveloped by Anthropic went rogue and
OL,8,Fsent US police a fake tip about an
OL,9,Funsolved murder earlier this year,
OL,10,Fauthorities have revealed.
OL,12,FThe Philadelphia Police Department said
OL,13,Fthe 18 July tip was "flagged as spam"
OL,14,Fand not passed on for investigation -
OL,15,Fbut the force criticised the tech firm
OL,16,Ffor taking more than two months to
OL,17,Fdetect and report the breach.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,109,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1791778697
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,ARogue Anthropic AI agent gave police
OL,4,Afake tip in unsolved murder case
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt said the bogus tip came through a
OL,7,Fpublic website where people can share
OL,8,Finformation on unsolved murders, and
OL,9,Fthat the AI agent had claimed to have
OL,10,Fseen "someone matching the
OL,11,Fdescription".
OL,13,FIt is believed to be the first time an
OL,14,FAI agent has sent fabricated
OL,15,Finformation to authorities, but is the
OL,16,Flatest in a series of incidents
OL,17,Finvolving rogue AI activity, including
OL,18,Fhacking systems or taking control of
OL,19,Fplatforms.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/19
